          "id": "678de86a48480971bb23faec9af40c589aa94253",
          "message": "fix(qwen4_exp): keep the PLE table BF16 for Quark checkpoints (#2595)\n\nQuark's exclude list names only linear modules, so the PLE n-gram\nembedding of amd/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Quark-MXFP4 falls under the MXFP4\nglobal spec and the model refused to build (\"PLE embedding supports BF16\nor FP8 checkpoints\"), although the checkpoint stores the table in BF16.\n\nInfer FP8 PLE storage from the quantization policy only for FP8\ncheckpoints, as before; any other format builds a BF16 table and the\nshard loader still rejects a checkpoint whose PLE dtype differs.\n\nWith this, the Quark MXFP4 checkpoint serves at TP1 and scores 0.9765\n(flexible) / 0.9757 (strict) on GSM8K, 5-shot chat, per\nrecipes/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
