          "id": "9955d15301856c43661b01711380e664eb26c78e",
          "message": "fix(v41): declare TR-graph breaks inside the boundary ops (#2690)\n\n#2688 made `begin_forward`, `end_forward` and `engram_forward` TR-graph\nbreaks by decorating the methods with `eager_region()`. Those methods are\ncalled from `_EarlyLayers` / `_LateLayers`, which are torch.compiled, and\n`eager_region` calls straight through while Dynamo traces. The compiled\nstage then calls `torch.ops.aiter.v41_begin_forward` / `v41_engram`\ndirectly, so no break happens at replay or record time.\n\nRecording the prefill token graphs, the Engram staging fork\n(`EngramStaging.start`: `stream.wait_stream(compute)`) lands inside the\nfirst segment, its join is in `v41_end_forward` at the end of the forward,\nand the first real break (layer 0's `_compress`) ends a capture with an\nunjoined stream: `hipErrorStreamCaptureUnjoined` at server start\n(DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash DSpark accuracy CI on main).\n\nPut `eager_region()` under `torch_compile_guard` on the three ops, as\n`dspark_block_attention`, `kda_attention_with_output` and\n`unified_attention_with_output_base` already do, and drop the method-level\ndecorators that compilation discards. The test fake forward context gains\n`main_stream` / `in_hipgraph`, which an unrecorded break reads.\n\nValidation (CI image rocm/atom-dev:nightly_202610231620 + CI aiter wheel,\nMI355X TP4, --kv_cache_dtype bf16 --index_cache_dtype fp4 --method dspark\n--num-speculative-tokens 5):\n- before: same hipErrorStreamCaptureUnjoined as CI\n- after: prefill token graphs (256..3072) and request graphs recorded,\n  server ready; GSM8K 3-shot flexible 0.9257 / strict 0.9265\n- black, ruff clean; tests/test_region_graph.py, tests/attentions/deepseek_v41,\n  tests/models/deepseek_v41 and the V4.1/Engram tests: 1504 passed\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-24T11:23:53+08:00",
