          "distinct": true,
          "id": "4f6ce2f9a96ce3a8c7f83cbe0a8a3d3077648067",
          "message": "perf(engram): copy the UVA shard into page-locked memory instead of registering the mapping (#2684)\n\n* perf(engram): copy the UVA shard into page-locked memory instead of registering the mapping\n\nThe UVA lookup page-locked this rank's head shard of each Engram table by\nhipHostRegister on the checkpoint mapping. The mapping is private, so\nregistration copies every page on its write fault, on one thread, while\nholding the HIP runtime lock -- which also stalls the rest of startup.\n\nenable_uva now allocates page-locked memory of exactly the shard's size with\nhipHostMalloc (via ctypes: torch's pinned allocator rounds to a power of two\nand holds the GIL) and copies the rows on 16 threads. The kernel addresses\nonly the shard, so registered_shard returns the copies and nothing else\nchanges; disable_uva frees them. The memory is the same as before: the\nregistered pages were anonymous copies too.\n\nATOM_ENGRAM_UVA_COPY=0 keeps the in-place registration; without the HIP\nruntime the shard is registered in place regardless.\n\n* fix(engram): free the pinned shard on any copy failure; keep tests off the real allocator\n\n- _copy_into_pinned frees every allocation and returns False on any failure\n  (no memory, no thread to copy on, a copy error), so disable_uva has nothing\n  stranded and EngramHost's group vote can fall back as one.\n- An autouse fixture keeps every engram test off the real hipHostMalloc on\n  ROCm runners; the in-place registration tests script cudaHostRegister and\n  the copy tests install their own fake allocator.\n\n* refactor(engram): page-locked shard owned by its tensors, in a host-memory module\n\n- host_memory.pin_rows owns allocation, copy and release. Each region is a\n  lease held by the storage of every tensor over it: released with the last\n  tensor (never while registered_shard's result is alive), and released when\n  a table is dropped without disable_uva. hipHostFree / unregister synchronize\n  the device first; a release during graph capture is skipped with a warning.\n- tables.py keeps one shard (tensors) and its row range; enabling a\n  different range while one is held raises.\n- Copy: one copy_ below 128 MiB, else one memmove thread per 128 MiB, at most\n  16 and the CPUs in this process's affinity; torch's thread count untouched.\n- Copied checkpoint pages are dropped from the process chunk by chunk\n  (madvise DONTNEED on file mappings only): the shard is resident once.\n  Before, the copy and its source were both resident (2x shard).\n- hipHostMalloc runs with transparent huge pages disabled: on a page cache\n  fragmented by checkpoint loading it compacted memory for ~197 s per TP2\n  rank (143k compaction stalls); ~12 s on base pages, gather unchanged.\n- tools/engram/bench_uva_shard.py and bench_host_copy.py reproduce the\n  per-rank timings, memory and gather latency; docs updated.\n\n* fix(engram): keep a shard released during capture, drop only unmodified source pages, chunk the one-worker copy\n\n* test(engram): the failing-copy stub takes drop, so the scripted error is what is raised\n\n* fix(engram): check every mapping a source range touches before dropping its pages\n\n* perf(engram): check source pages per chunk in pagemap instead of scanning smaps\n\n/proc/self/smaps walks the page tables of every mapping in the process:\n~0.36 s per call in a GPU process (1288 mappings), four calls per rank.\nNow /proc/self/maps (~1 ms) checks the range is one file without gaps, and\neach chunk's own pages are checked in /proc/self/pagemap on the copy thread\njust before it is dropped (~10 ms per GiB): a page written through a private\nmapping is anonymous and keeps its chunk, whatever the mapping's protection\nor how mprotect split it -- exact per page rather than per mapping. Chunks\nare cut at page boundaries so the final whole-range drop is gone.\n\n* fix(engram): wait for every copy chunk before the dropper closes; a closed dropper does nothing\n\n* fix(engram): drain the copy pool when a submit fails; closing the dropper waits for drops in progress\n\n* fix(engram): a raising table votes no; one copy_ below 512 MiB as documented; docstrings for the copy path\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ZhangLirong-amd <ZhangLirong-amd@users.noreply.github.com>",
