          "id": "29fbf7b25e1a06798667f3b84451b9e640e0234f",
          "message": "ci(agentic): run the DSv4.1 DTP2/DEP2 c128 cells with InferenceX's DPA recipe (#2784)\n\n* ci(agentic): run the DSv4.1 DTP2/DEP2 c128 cells with InferenceX's DPA recipe\n\n#2696 added the DTP2 and DEP2 c128 cells on the model-wide flags only. The\nInferenceX DSv4.1 ATOM AgentX DPA run (SemiAnalysisAI/InferenceX run\n40362093275, TP2/DPA c128) also sets the DPA scheduling knobs. Without them a\nprefill can land on almost every step: our 10-26 nightly DTP2 c128 reached\n1334 output tok/s/GPU at 37.3 ms mean ITL, InferenceX 2123 at 15.8 ms.\n\nBoth DPA variants now match that recipe:\n- env: ATOM_PREFILL_DECODE_INTERVAL=10, ATOM_DP_SESSION_AFFINITY=1,\n  ATOM_DP_LB_REQ_EQUIV=512, ATOM_ENABLE_PREFILL_DELAYER=1, GPU_MAX_HW_QUEUES=5\n- args: --dp-load-balance least_tokens, --kv_cache_dtype bf16,\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9, capture sizes up to 128\n\nVariant args follow the model-wide ones, so the TP2/TP4 cells are unchanged.\n\n* ci(agentic): keep the model-wide KV cache dtype for the DSv4.1 DPA cells\n\n* ci(agentic): drop GPU_MAX_HW_QUEUES and the default prefill-delayer flag from the DSv4.1 DPA cells",
