          "id": "59f6b5d388dbefbe7d1c7d93db5c2af3bc716b95",
          "message": "fix(k3-mono): read o_norm as native fp32 and accept bf16 latent projections (#2841)\n\nThe model holds the KDA o_norm weight in fp32 (control_dtype), so bind it as is\nand read it with ld_f32 in kda_norm instead of ld_bf; a bf16 o_norm is refused.\nA bf16 checkpoint has no weight_scale on the latent down/up projections, so\n_mxfp4_to_bf16 passes them through (up band still copied) instead of failing.\nAdds CPU tests for both paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
