          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e2e175c08d9b33e16a4cc35df31515507dd14104",
          "message": "ci: avoid restarting tests on PR approval (#2374)\n\n* Approvals CI fix\n\n* ci: let an approval take over a pending PR run it replaced\n\nA concurrency group keeps one pending run, so an approval that arrives\nwhile the PR run is still waiting on a previous run replaces it before\nany job starts. Heavy CI still ran once, from the approval, but the\noffline smoke test for that head SHA was never run.\n\nThe gate now detects this case on approval events: the latest same-SHA\npull_request run was cancelled without creating any jobs, and no later\nreview run has published the smoke check. It then sets\nreplaced_pr_run=true and atom-test runs the smoke test under its real\ncheck name. Only atom-test opts in through CI_GATE_PR_CHECK_JOB; vLLM\nand SGLang have no PR-only checks.\n\n* ci: rename smoke takeover output and skip it off main\n\n* ci: let approvals run heavy CI when Pre Checkin never passed\n\n* ci: give the skipped smoke job on review runs a readable name",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-04T13:25:42+08:00",
