          "id": "ab4ada40a2d9ffe1fb1cc50f95d85ce63ce92619",
          "message": "fix(attention): build sparse decode metadata over the padded batch (#2992)\n\nA TR_HYBRID decode replays at running_bs, the ladder rung above the\nscheduled batch, but the sparse block tables and seq_lens covered only\nscheduled_bs rows. The pad rows then read uninitialized tables and the\nreplay hit an illegal memory access whenever a step ran between rungs\n(e.g. 65-127 concurrent requests on the 128 graph).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-05T10:49:11+08:00",
