          "id": "0fe9932af84b6f9c359f18e90b685af13dab762f",
          "message": "fix(ci): run DeepSeek-V3.2-FP8 DP/EP on SGLang with ATOM_FUSE_SHARED_EXPERT=0 (#2986)\n\nUnder DP attention with MoRI EP, FusedMoE fuses the shared expert into the\nall-to-all layout only for MXFP4/NVFP4 routed experts. DeepSeek-V3.2's routed\nexperts are FP8, so the TP4 DP4 EP4 and TP8 DP8 EP8 cells failed at init with\n\"Shared-expert fusion is only wired up for the MXFP4 MoE path, got\nFp8MoEMethod\". Keep the shared expert a separate MLP there, as the docs and\nthe atomesh FP8 MoE cells already do.\n\nApplied to the SGLang accuracy workflow, its dashboard catalog and the SGLang\nbenchmark catalog, with a test that keeps them in sync.\n\nCo-authored-by: junyan.yang@amd.com <junyan.yang@amd.com@pit2-vm-amd-xl-02.amd.pit2.tensorwave.lan>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
