          "id": "75e6b9a4f3b2b0abc63aba003230c90080937b76",
          "message": "[gfx1250] Add ATOM_MLA_ABSORB_BF16: keep MLA-absorb weights in BF16 (#2489)\n\nPort of sglang #31604 for the ATOM gfx1250 path. On DeepSeek-R1 the MLA-absorb\nweights (W_K/W_V from kv_b_proj) are re-quantized to per-batched-tensor FP8,\nwhich costs MLPerf accuracy at the tight gate. ATOM_MLA_ABSORB_BF16=1 keeps\nW_K/W_V in BF16 (scale=None marker) and runs the absorbed bmm via the Triton\nbatched_gemm_bf16 kernel — gfx1250 hipBLASLt's bf16 batched GEMM (torch.bmm)\nmemory-faults, so torch.bmm is avoided. Default off (unchanged FP8 behavior).\n\nMLPerf DeepSeek-R1 (image 20261006): 79.83 (fp8) -> 80.54 (bf16), at the gate.\n\nCo-authored-by: karverma-amd <karverma-amd@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
