          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e48ad896f07e8a6de4018f66a94ae23c1b26dc54",
          "message": "feat(api): add DeepSeek's beta FIM and assistant-prefix completion (#3036)\n\n* feat(api): add DeepSeek's beta FIM and assistant-prefix completion\n\nPart 2 of #2864, BETA-01 and BETA-02.\n\n/beta/completions takes `suffix` and renders the model's fill-in-the-middle\nformat, found by its markers each encoding to a single token. It also\ntakes DeepSeek's `echo` (leading the first streamed chunk) and\n`stream_options`: with `include_usage` every chunk carries `usage` and a\nusage chunk precedes [DONE], and without it the stream carries no usage.\n`logprobs` (0 to 20) is refused until completions return token\nprobabilities.\n\n/beta/chat/completions continues a final assistant message marked\n`prefix: true`: earlier messages render as for an ordinary request and the\nprefix is appended to the opened assistant turn. When the reply begins in\nthe reasoning channel -- the server's own reading, so a model that starts\nthere with no marker, like DeepSeek-R1, counts -- a `reasoning_content`\nprefix continues the chain of thought and a content prefix closes it\nfirst. On Kimi-K3's channel format the response channel is opened before\nthe content.\n\nBoth beta routes take `stop` as one string or a list, and are timed and\ntraced like the /v1 routes. /v1 is unchanged: its request models do not\ndeclare the new parameters, so they are ignored there as before, and a\n`prefix` flag on /v1 is ignored too. The mesh router does not route the\nbeta endpoints yet.\n\n* fix(api): stream /beta/completions usage as DeepSeek documents it\n\nDeepSeek's stream ends with the finish chunk carrying the request's usage,\nwith or without `include_usage`, and sends no usage-only chunk;\n`include_usage` only adds `usage: null` to the chunks before it.\n/beta/completions sent the usage-only chunk on request and no usage at\nall otherwise.\n\nChat already streams this shape on a V4.1 deployment through\n`chat_usage_on_finish`. /beta/completions now takes the same deployment\nchoice, renamed `usage_on_finish` since it covers completions too.\n/v1/completions and other deployments keep the usage-only chunk.\n\n* fix(api): read a continued answer as the answer; take max_tokens 0 on /beta/completions\n\nA content prefix in thinking mode closes the reasoning channel in the\nprompt, but the reader was told only that the output does not begin inside\nthe channel, so it read the continuation as text before the channel: think\ntags the model then wrote came back as reasoning_content. continue_prompt\nnow returns the channel to read the continuation with, and\nReasoningChannel.answer_started starts the reader after the channel, where\nthe format's answer framing (Kimi-K3) is still removed and think markers\nare the model's own words, as when the model closes the channel itself.\n\nDeepSeek's completions take max_tokens >= 0. /beta/completions answers 0\nwithout the engine: the echo alone (or empty text), finish_reason length,\nthe prompt tokenized as the engine would for its usage and the context\ncheck, through the same response builders and streamed-usage contract.\n/v1/completions still requires at least 1.\n\n* fix(api): a content prefix begins the answer with thinking off too; no TTFT for max_tokens 0\n\ncontinue_prompt marked the answer as begun only when it closed the\nreasoning channel itself. With thinking off (V4.1's chat mode renders\n`</think>` into the prompt) a content prefix has begun the answer just the\nsame, but the reader started before the channel, so think tags the model\nthen wrote came back as reasoning_content. Any non-empty content prefix now\nstarts the reader in the answer; an empty one still reads as an ordinary\nreply.\n\nA max_tokens 0 completion generates nothing, but its echoed prompt went out\nas the first text frame and was recorded as a time to first token. It now\nrecords none.\n\n* fix(api): join an assistant prefix's text blocks as the encoder joins them\n\nA prefix's content list was joined by get_content_text, one line apart,\nbefore it was appended to the render. That is how every message reaches a\nchat template, but DeepSeek-V4.1's encoder is given content lists intact\nand joins their text blocks a blank line apart (process_image_messages), so\na multi-block prefix did not match the official unterminated assistant\nturn. The adapter now carries its encoder's rule (join_text_blocks), and the\nprefix is joined by it when there is one; get_content_text is unchanged for\nthe chat-template path. The official-encoder differential test covers text\nblocks too.\n\n* fix(api): pass an assistant prefix through the encoder's own message processing; prefix null is unset\n\nThe last commit copied DeepSeek-V4.1's text-block joining into ATOM, but the\nofficial process_image_messages also refuses image placeholder tokens in a\nmessage's content, text blocks and reasoning_content. A prefix skipped that\ncheck, so an assistant message the history refuses (400 on /v1) went into\nthe /beta prompt as typed. The loader now hands the module's\nprocess_image_messages to the adapter, and the prefix goes through it as the\nrendered messages do: joining and the check both come from the official\nimplementation. join_text_blocks is gone.\n\n`prefix: null` on any message is now read as unset rather than a 400.\n\nThe official-encoder differential test gains the content-only prefix in\nthinking mode, where this server closes the reasoning channel itself, and a\ntest that a prefix refuses image placeholders as the history does.",
