          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f64eed0e01283343784bb47e27552f11b1de2bd0",
          "message": "perf(qwen4_exp): keep the PLE n-gram table in page-locked host memory, read over UVA (#2771)\n\n* perf(qwen4_exp): keep the PLE n-gram table in page-locked host memory, read over UVA\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* qwen4_exp PLE: follow #2754's HIP runtime and page runs\n\n- device_address asks the HIP runtime host_memory page-locks with\n  (`_hip_runtime`, torch's), not `CDLL(\"libamdhip64.so\")`, which can be a\n  second runtime that does not know those allocations.\n- Drop the GPU lookup tests' in-place `register` mode. The PLE table never\n  registers in place (pin_rows(copy=True)), and since #2754 in-place\n  registrations of adjacent unaligned shards share their boundary pages, so\n  a shard spans separately mapped device ranges and cannot be read from one\n  base address -- the merged test faulted for exactly that reason.\n- Test pin_rows' `copy` override: it beats ATOM_ENGRAM_UVA_COPY and `shared`,\n  and a refused `copy=False` does not fall back to a copy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-10T15:08:05+08:00",
