          "id": "99aa67e2f566414937235d17053cd63a76066c78",
          "message": "fix(plugin): start DeepSeek-V4.1 on the vLLM plugin again after #3136 (#3189)\n\n* vllm plugin: call h2d_group_members, now a method, for V4.1\n\n#3136 made AttentionMetadataBuilder.h2d_group_members a method, but the\nV4.1 publication wrapper in the plugin still read it as a dict, so every\nDeepSeek-V4.1 serve on the vLLM plugin failed in profile_run:\n\n    v41_core_overrides.py:87, in publish\n        for name, names in self.h2d_group_members.items():\n    AttributeError: 'function' object has no attribute 'items'\n\nThe wrapper only needs the groups V4.1 publishes by name outside TBO\n(step_metadata from the builder, the producer groups from the buffers),\nwhich the method returns.\n\nThe new test checks the plugin source, since the non-GPU unit run cannot\nimport the module that broke.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* vllm plugin: keep V4.1 dummy verify buckets non-verifying\n\n#3136 changed native `_prepare_step` from\n`verifying = tentative and not batch.is_dummy_run and bool(spans)` to\n`verifying = tentative and bool(spans)`: native capture batches are not\ndummies. The plugin's warmup before a DSpark capture is: its dummy batch\nis fabricated on private scratch with every request at position 0, and\n`_v41_prepare_kwargs` marks a uniform verify-width batch tentative so the\nplan keeps the verify write grid. `begin_step` now refuses that step and\nevery DeepSeek-V4.1 DSpark serve on the plugin fails at capture:\n\n    ValueError: Tentative verification needs a prefix and sufficient\n    window slack\n\nBegin that one step as non-verifying, as before #3136; the plan still\ngets the verify write grid from `tentative`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* vllm plugin: say that a V4.1 dummy verify bucket runs the prefill FFN\n\nReview on #3189: forcing the dummy's step to non-verifying also makes it\na prefill step (`BatchStep.decode`), so it runs the prefill FFN rather\nthan `decode_ffn`. That is how it ran before #3136 and is intended: dummy\nbatches only feed eager forwards whose output is discarded, while the\nbatches captures record are not dummies and stay verifying. Docstring\nonly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: perzhang <perzhang@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
