          "id": "3659b98656615448b3a4982289a0d9b37b67b27e",
          "message": "perf(dsv41): widen the indexer block-maxima grid and use 128-wide candidate tiles (#3128)\n\n* perf(dsv41): widen the indexer block-maxima grid and use 128-wide candidate tiles\n\n_block_maxima_kernel is one load and one max per tile, so a program has\nlittle latency of its own to hide; the grid now targets more programs in\nflight. pick_candidate_blocks(_packed) default to 128-wide candidate\ntiles. Selection results are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dsv41): keep the wider maxima grid and 128-wide tile to gfx1250\n\nThe wider block-maxima grid and the 128-wide candidate tile were tuned on\ngfx1250 only. Select them at runtime on gfx1250 and keep the previous\nlane target and tile on other archs, with the original docstring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
