          "id": "a11bb34c8004f4c2497597cc907b70ae5fa63674",
          "message": "fix(kimi-k3.1): include DSA index keys in offload (#3063)\n\n* fix(kimi-k3): offload the DSA index keys with the MLA rows\n\nKimi-K3's MLA binder bound each layer's DSA index slice onto the indexer but\nleft it off the `KVCacheTensor`, and the dense offload codec reads nothing\nelse. A prefix restored from an offload tier (`lmcache_offload`) therefore got\nits MLA rows back while its pages kept the index keys of whichever request held\nthem before, and the indexer ranked those stale keys when it chose the sparse\ntop-k. HBM prefix hits never saw it, since a page keeps both; P/D does not\neither, since it moves the published PAGE regions.\n\nPublish the slice on the `KVCacheTensor`, as the plain MLA builder\n(aiter_mla.py) already does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mla): share cache binding across hybrid builders\n\nExtract the MLA KV/index binding into the parent builder so Kimi Aiter and Triton preserve FP4 scale publication and the indexer layout check. Keep the hybrid kpool tail binding in Kimi, and run the cache binding regressions across all three builders.\n\n* fix(kimi-k3): keep offload index publication fix minimal\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
