          "message": "fix(attention): drop the FlyDSL paged-decode API probe (#3108)\n\n* fix(attention): keep FlyDSL paged decode on aiter's optional work plan\n\naiter #7056 gave pa_decode's keyword `work_plan` a default of None, so MXFP4\nK/V can run without a plan. ATOM's probe for the #5809 API also required the\nplan to have no default, so with current aiter it reported \"this aiter\npredates the #5809 decode API\" and routed every FlyDSL paged decode to gluon,\neven with ATOM_PA_FLYDSL=1.\n\nThe default never told the two APIs apart: before #5809 `work_plan` was a\npositional, optional argument and pa_decode took no `max_context_length`,\nand plan_pa_decode did not exist in that module. Keep those checks and drop\nthe default one. ATOM still passes a plan on every call, which current aiter\nrequires for non-MXFP4 K/V.\n\n* fix(attention): probe only #5809's API markers for FlyDSL paged decode\n\nDrop the remaining check on how work_plan is declared (keyword-only): like\nits default, it is incidental to the API, and a change to it would again\nroute FlyDSL paged decode to gluon with only a warning. max_context_length\nseparates #5809's pa_decode from the earlier one; plan_pa_decode is what\nATOM calls. Fold the probe tests into one parametrized test.\n\n* fix(attention): drop the FlyDSL paged-decode API probe\n\nThe probe only guarded aiter older than #5809, which no CI image or recipe\nuses, and its signature checks silently routed every ATOM_PA_FLYDSL=1 decode\nto gluon once aiter changed an incidental property of pa_decode. Remove\n_flydsl_explicit_plan_api, its checks in _flydsl_pa_decode_num_seqs and the\nMiniMax-M3 startup validation, and their tests.\n\n* fix(attention): drop the max_batch_size probe from the FlyDSL plan cap\n\naiter added gfx1250 FlyDSL paged decode and plan_pa_decode's max_batch_size\ntogether (#6462), so the signature check could only ever fail on a future\nrename, silently capping gfx1250 plans at 4096. Gate on the arch alone and\nstop importing the planner on every other GPU.",
