          "distinct": true,
          "id": "91128a94636154df71104866e4ffc590dba0aa55",
          "message": "perf(dsv41): fold the shared-expert add into the MoE TP all-reduce via HIP Lamport kernel (#3020)\n\n* perf(dsv41): fold the shared-expert add into the MoE TP all-reduce\n\n`MoE.combine_outputs` added the shared expert into the routed output and then\nall-reduced the sum. At TP > 1 it now calls\n`tensor_model_parallel_all_reduce_add(routed, shared)`, which aiter's gfx1250\nGluon all-reduce serves in one kernel with the same bits (the add happens as\nthe reduce loads its input). Where aiter has no fused op, on the TBO path, or\noutside the Gluon path, it is the add followed by the plain all-reduce, as\nbefore.\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash TP4 C8 decode (48 rows x 5120 bf16): 7.60 -> 6.03 us per\nMoE layer, ~70 us per 9.55 ms step over 43 layers.\n\nNeeds the aiter all-reduce add (karverma-amd/aiter karverma/gfx1250-allreduce-fused-residual-add);\nwithout it this falls back to the add followed by the plain all-reduce.\n\n* test(dsv41): fused all-reduce add vs add + all-reduce, bit for bit\n\nReview on #3020: name the aiter op (ROCm/aiter#7488) and its semantics in\nthe wrapper, and check the numerics. The fused op is the sum over ranks of\neach rank's x + y, the same bits as all-reducing the materialized sum.\n\ntests/model_ops/test_all_reduce_add_gpu.py (4 gfx1250 GPUs, skips elsewhere):\ntensor_model_parallel_all_reduce_add(routed, shared) against\ntensor_model_parallel_all_reduce(routed + shared) at 5120 bf16, rows 1-409\n(fused Gluon kernel, asserted to run) and 410/4096 (fallback), equal on\nevery rank, eager and over HIP graph replays.\n\n* perf(dsv41): serve the fused MoE all-reduce add with the HIP Lamport kernel\n\nThe shared-expert add still goes through tensor_model_parallel_all_reduce_add.\naiter#7499 serves that op with the gfx1250 HIP one-shot kernel. The test now\nrequires lamport_ar_add for every row count the kernel accepts, including a\nHIP-graph capture, and checks the bits against add plus all-reduce.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* test(dsv41): pin the Lamport all-reduce cap to the TP4 8 MiB default\n\nThe row search used to stop at whatever should_lamport_ar_add accepted, so a wrong cap still passed. The unset TP4 limit is 819 rows, and the probe now stops at 4096.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Call aiter's all-reduce add directly.\n\nATOM no longer probes for tensor_model_parallel_all_reduce_add. The TBO path still adds and all-reduces here; aiter#7499 owns kernel eligibility and the other fallback.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Verma, Karan <Karan.Verma+amdeng@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: karverma-amd <karverma-amd@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
